<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Healthy Minds for Healthy Bodies – Lesson # 1</h2>
<p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Checking in on Health</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Healthy Minds for Healthy Bodies</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Demonstrate comprehension of extended discussions on abstract topics. Interactive: Simulate negotiation scenarios in various settings.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can demonstrate understanding of extended discussions about health technologies and long-term habits (e.g., "I have been using a fitness app to improve my workout routine.")
Can identify key points in conversations about mental health practices (e.g., "You might need to practice mindfulness to reduce stress.")
Can follow a simulated negotiation between a patient and a health coach about creating a fitness plan (e.g., "I can exercise three times a week, but I prefer yoga over running.")</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher begins by projecting images related to various healthy habits and mental well-being practices (e.g., someone meditating, exercising, a healthy meal, a fitness app screenshot). Students, in pairs, briefly discuss which images represent "healthy minds" and "healthy bodies." The teacher then introduces 8-10 core vocabulary words on the board: <b>well-being, mindfulness, habits, stress, nutrition, lifestyle, app, practice, manage, improve</b>. Students share one current healthy habit they have been practicing, using the phrase "I have been [verb-ing]..." (e.g., "I have been drinking more water.").</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of the new vocabulary words, paying special attention to the target sounds. For example, contrasting /b/ in "<b>b</b>alance" and "<b>b</b>oost" (not a core word, but good for contrast) with /p/ in "<b>p</b>ractice" and "<b>p</b>revent". The teacher also models /s/ in "<b>s</b>tress" and "<b>s</b>leep" and /z/ in "e<b>x</b>ercise." Emphasis is placed on sentence rhythm when using the present perfect continuous, highlighting content words like "drinking" and reducing "have" (/həv/) in "I have been drinking more water." The teacher demonstrates how to express empathy with phrases like, "That sounds tough. I hope you're resting," and suggests tips politely, "You might want to try meditation."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher uses CCQs and examples to ensure understanding of key terms and concepts related to listening for health advice.
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If someone says, 'I have been practicing mindfulness,' what does 'mindfulness' mean? Is it about being stressed or being present and aware?" (Expected answer: Present and aware.)</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'You might want to try this healthy habit,' am I forcing you, or just giving a suggestion? What tone should I use?" (Expected answer: Giving a suggestion, polite tone.)</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Audio recording of a simulated conversation (approximately 2-3 minutes) between a patient (Elena) checking in on her health and a health coach (Mr. Johnson). The conversation includes discussions about using a fitness <b>app</b>, practicing <b>mindfulness</b>, changing eating <b>habits</b>, and managing <b>stress</b>. It uses Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, and modals for possibility. (e.g., "I have been using a fitness app," "If I had more free time, I would join a yoga class," "You might need to drink more water.")</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening: Can understand the main points of clear standard speech on familiar matters regularly encountered in work, school, leisure, etc., including short narratives.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>First listening (Gist):</b> Students listen to the conversation once and answer: "What is the main topic of Elena and Mr. Johnson's conversation?" (A. Planning a vacation, B. Discussing Elena's health and lifestyle, C. Booking a doctor's appointment).</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Second listening (True/False & Key points):</b> Students listen again and decide if the following statements are True or False. They also identify two key practices Elena has been doing.
              <ol>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Elena has been sleeping eight hours every night. (T/F)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Mr. Johnson suggests Elena could try mindfulness exercises. (T/F)</li>
              </ol>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Listening)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice identifying Present Perfect Continuous for ongoing health efforts, Second Conditional for hypothetical well-being improvements, and modals for possibility when suggesting health strategies. Focus on target vocabulary: <b>well-being, mindfulness, habits, stress, nutrition, lifestyle, app, practice, manage, improve</b>.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Cloze Listening):</b> The teacher provides a transcript excerpt of the conversation with 5-7 blanks corresponding to the target vocabulary words (e.g., "...I've been using a new fitness _______ to track my activity level.") or grammatical structures (e.g., "...If I ______ (have) more time, I ______ (would/could) join a yoga class."). Students listen to the audio a third time and fill in the blanks.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Identifying Suggestions):</b> Students listen to specific segments of the audio again. Their task is to identify and write down three health suggestions Mr. Johnson gives Elena, paying attention to the modals used (e.g., "You might need...", "You could try..."). They underline the modal verb and the health advice given.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction (Verification & Discussion):</b> In pairs, students compare their filled-in cloze passages and identified suggestions. They discuss why certain words or phrases were used, specifically focusing on how the Present Perfect Continuous highlights ongoing actions and how the Second Conditional implies hypothetical situations. They practice expressing empathy by listening to each other's answers and politely suggesting corrections if needed (e.g., "You might have missed this word; I heard 'mindfulness'.").</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">12-15 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task:</b> Simulated Health Negotiation Role-play.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in pairs. One student takes the role of a "Patient" who is checking in on their health and expresses current habits and potential areas for <b>improve</b>ment, including concerns about <b>stress</b> or lack of <b>well-being</b>. The other student acts as a "Health Coach" who listens actively and offers polite health suggestions, using modals for possibility (e.g., "You might want to consider...", "You could try..."). The patient must listen carefully to the suggestions and negotiate a realistic plan, using second conditionals to explain preferences (e.g., "If I had more free time, I would try a yoga class, but I can only exercise two times a week"). The focus is on active <b>listening</b> to understand needs and suggestions, and then negotiating based on that understanding. Students should incorporate at least 3 vocabulary words (e.g., <b>lifestyle, nutrition, mindfulness</b>) and at least one instance of Present Perfect Continuous and Second Conditional each in their dialogue. They should also practice giving polite suggestions and showing empathy.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment during the role-play.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students perform the "Simulated Health Negotiation Role-play."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Active Listening:</b> Did the "Patient" respond appropriately to the "Coach's" suggestions? Did the "Coach" address the "Patient's" concerns?</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Vocabulary:</b> Incorporated at least 3 specified vocabulary words correctly (e.g., well-being, mindfulness, stress).</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar Accuracy:</b> Correct use of Present Perfect Continuous and Second Conditional.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pragmatic Competence:</b> Giving polite health suggestions (modals) and expressing empathy.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and Intelligibility:</b> Pronunciation of key sounds (/b/, /p/, /s/, /z/) and sentence rhythm for PPC phrases is clear.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b>
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new health suggestion you heard or made today that you found interesting?"</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How effectively did you listen to your partner's needs/suggestions during the role-play?"</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">6-8 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was challenging about listening to specific details in the conversations today, and how can you improve your listening skills?"</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which of the new vocabulary words or grammar points do you feel most confident using now?"</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The listening activities were effective in introducing new vocabulary and grammar. Students engaged well with the negotiation role-play, showing good listening comprehension and interactive skills. Some students might need additional practice with distinguishing between /s/ and /z/ sounds, and sentence rhythm for the present perfect continuous. For the next lesson, I will provide a reading text that reinforces these vocabulary words and grammatical structures, setting the stage for deeper contextual understanding.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 2, students will read an article related to "Healthy Minds for Healthy Bodies" which will build upon the vocabulary and concepts introduced in this listening lesson, allowing them to encounter the same language in a different context.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>